description:
FILED s522b (Opus, 2026-10-19) from member 4 (#1506)'s probes (Fable's b5 r3).  The static-parse limit (docs/static-parse-limits-review-s512.md family 1/2): perl learns the `()` prototype by RUNNING the BEGIN; PCL's parser never sees it.

    BEGIN { require constant; constant->import({ H1 => 3, H2 => 4 }) } print "r3 ", H1 + H2, "\n";

perl: r3 7.  PCL (with s522b's lib/constant.pm): `r3 3` and no newline -- H1 is a list operator swallowing `+H2, "\n"`.  `H1() + H2()` is right (the guard row uses that spelling).  The #2610 detector (PCL_DETECT, default announce) says nothing: worth checking why the run-time install does not reach the override recorder -- a silent wrong where the detector should speak.  Not the shim's fault; any BEGIN-time `*{...} = sub () {...}` has it.
